    intro: 'A health and disease game where you do instead of choose. In “Stop the outbreak” there is a grid of people with one sick person and some immune: you vaccinate three and run the infection, which passes from neighbour to neighbour, generation by generation; well-placed vaccines act as a firebreak. With a slider you find what share of the population must be vaccinated for each sick person to infect fewer than one (1 − 1/R₀). There is also completing a disease card —which microbe causes it, drawn, and how it spreads— and sorting microbes, infectious or non-infectious diseases, whether antibiotics work, lines of defence and types of immunity.',
